---
layout: base.njk
navyHeader: true
pagination:
  data: insights
  size: 1
  alias: post
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/insights/{{ post.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ post.title }} — Admizz Group"
  description: "{{ post.deck }}"
---

{# ============================================================================
   /insights/<slug>/ — rebuilt 2026-08-27. Previously rendered the entire
   article body as ONE <p> with no reading time, despite the readingTime
   filter already existing (used elsewhere, unused here) and the article
   page being the obvious place for it.

   post.bodyParagraphs (insights.json, new field, post.body left untouched)
   splits each article into 2 real paragraphs. This is typesetting, not
   invented content — same sentences, same order, just where the breaks
   fall; the source copy (insights.json's `body`) never had paragraph
   breaks of its own to preserve.
   ============================================================================ #}

{# Reading progress: a 2px bar, scaled by main.js on scroll. With no JS it
   simply never grows — nothing on the page depends on it. #}
<div class="read-progress" data-read-progress aria-hidden="true"></div>

<section class="insights-hero bg-navy-deep py-section-sm">
  {# Large faint Admizz mark — simple, on purpose: the real brand mark
     (same asset the header uses inverted, and /ventures/'s field diagram
     crops), not a per-venture icon or number that needed explaining.
     Kept plain: no bespoke draw-in, just the same on-load fade the rest
     of this masthead already uses (data-hero-in). #}
  <img src="/assets/images/brand/mark-white.png" alt="" width="1024" height="308"
    class="insights-hero-mark" data-hero-in aria-hidden="true">

  <div class="shell relative"><div class="page-canvas">
    <a href="/insights/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-navy-on-muted hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature fade-up">
      <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 7H2M6 3L2 7l4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      All insights
    </a>
    {# Venture + reading time as one meta line, not two disconnected labels
       -- was the venture as the eyebrow, then reading time floating alone
       below the deck paragraph with no visual relationship to it. No real
       author or publish date exists for these articles (nothing invented
       here per non-negotiable #1), so this pairing is the real, honest
       attribution this page has: matches the "{{ venture }} · {{ time }}"
       pattern already used for these same posts everywhere else on the
       site (the homepage insights list, /insights/ index cards). #}
    {# Research pieces say so here too, with their real source count —
       the same citations-driven marker used on /insights/, so a piece
       can't claim sourcing it doesn't carry. #}
    <span class="eyebrow-on-navy mt-7 fade-up" style="animation-delay:60ms">
      {{ post.venture }} &middot; {{ post.body | readingTime }} min read{% if post.citations %} &middot; {{ post.citations | length }} sources cited{% endif %}
    </span>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-navy-on max-w-[20ch] text-balance fade-up" style="animation-delay:120ms">{{ post.title }}</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-navy-on-muted max-w-measure fade-up" style="animation-delay:180ms">{{ post.deck }}</p>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="bg-paper py-section">
  <div class="shell"><div class="page-canvas page-canvas-reading grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_15rem] gap-10 md:gap-14">
    {# data-hero-in, not .fade-up: this block sits right at the fold under
       the navy masthead, so .fade-up's scroll-gated reveal left it at
       opacity:0 (invisible, not just unrendered) on an ordinary viewport
       height until the visitor scrolled — reading as a blank section
       right after load. data-hero-in animates in on page load instead
       (same generic, page-agnostic hook the homepage hero uses in
       main.js), so it's already visible by the time anyone scrolls down
       to it. Still fully visible by default with no CSS hiding of its
       own — GSAP sets the hidden state itself only once it has loaded. #}
    <div data-hero-in>
      {# aspect ratio + object-cover: was rendering the source photo
         uncropped at its native aspect, with no consistent framing against
         the rest of the site's article imagery. (The watermark that used
         to sit in these source photos' corner -- see 2026-09-03 note on
         insights.json's images -- is now physically cropped out of the
         source files themselves, so no object-position bias is needed
         here.) #}
      <div class="overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep mb-10 aspect-[16/10] [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:block [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
        {% imageEager "src/assets/images/insights/" + post.image, post.imageAlt, "(min-width: 768px) 60vw, 100vw" %}
      </div>

      {# | safe (2026-09-08): the new research-tagged articles (source:
         "research") cite sources inline as real <a> links, matching the
         exact pattern already used in marketContext.json's `analysis`
         field (also rendered `| safe`) -- authored content, not visitor
         input, so this isn't an XSS risk the way escaping user text would
         be. The 3 original marketing-tagged posts have no markup in their
         paragraphs, so this is a no-op for them. #}
      <div class="insights-article-prose">
        {% for para in post.bodyParagraphs %}
        <p>{{ para | safe }}</p>

        {# Key figures land after the opening paragraph, where the piece has
           set up its subject but not yet made its case — the numbers the
           article exists to make were previously plain grey body text.
           Each keeps its own publisher link, the same "figure with its
           provenance directly beneath it" pattern already proven by
           .market-stat on /ventures/, rather than a new device. Driven by
           post.keyFigures, so the marketing-sourced articles (which have
           none) simply don't render this. #}
        {% if loop.first and post.keyFigures %}
        <div class="article-figures">
          {% for f in post.keyFigures %}
          <div class="article-figure">
            <p class="article-figure-value font-display font-light tabular-nums text-ink">{{ f.value }}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ f.label }}</p>
            <a href="{{ f.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-2 inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-text link-underline">
              {{ f.publisher }}
              <svg width="9" height="9" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5.5M10 4v4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {% if post.citations %}
      <div class="source-tier mt-12">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
          <h2 class="font-display font-book text-h4 text-ink">Sources</h2>
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Read at the primary source before publication</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4">
          {% for c in post.citations %}
          <a href="{{ c.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 py-3 border-t border-rule group">
            <span class="text-small text-ink group-hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ c.label }}</span>
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 text-ink-faint"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5.5M10 4v4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-small text-ink-muted">
          How we handle figures across the whole site: <a href="/sources/" class="link-underline text-ink">Sources &amp; Methodology</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {# hrefLabel-style fix, same pattern as /ventures/ and /contact/: where
         there's no real URL (Institute — ventureHref is "#"), render a
         status, not a link dressed as one; real links get target=_blank +
         rel=noopener since they leave the site. #}
      {% for v in ventures %}{% if v.name == post.venture %}
      {% if v.href == "#" %}
      {# Was just {{ v.hrefLabel }} alone ("No public site yet") with no
         subject -- a design critique read it as an orphaned, unexplained
         note. The contact page's version of this same fallback already
         frames it with the venture name; matching that here. #}
      <p class="mt-8 text-small text-ink-faint">{{ post.venture }} &mdash; {{ v.hrefLabel }}</p>
      {% else %}
      <a href="{{ v.href }}" class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Explore {{ post.venture }}
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>

    <aside data-hero-in>
      <span class="eyebrow">More Insights</span>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col">
        {% for other in insights %}
        {% if other.slug != post.slug %}
        <a href="/insights/{{ other.slug }}/" class="py-4 border-t border-rule first:border-t-0 group">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ other.venture }}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-h4 font-display font-book text-ink group-hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ other.title }}</h3>
          <span class="mt-1 block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">{{ other.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
        </a>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div></div>
</section>

{# CLOSE — shared with the homepage/About/Ventures/Insights index
   (partials/cta-close.njk). This template previously had no closing CTA
   at all, ending cold on the "More Insights" sidebar (2026-09-07). #}
{% include "partials/cta-close.njk" %}
